-- 1124: Blog post — "PL-300 Power BI Data Analyst in Singapore: Exam Domains, Funding and Practice Exams"
--
--       Lead-in post for WSQ - Microsoft Power BI Data Analyst Associate (PL-300) (TGS-2023037468).
--       Backdated to 2025-09-19 (published, status 1). No LinkedIn / Facebook share is
--       performed: linkedin_urn carries the manual-skip sentinel and the post ships
--       already-published, so publishDue never picks it up.
--
-- Every figure below was read off the LIVE course page on 2026-08-26, not invented:
--   * Fee card: full $1,200.00, GST $108.00 (9%), baseline nett $708.00
--     (SG/PR 21+, 50%), MCES/SME nett $468.00 (SG 40+, 70%).
--   * Course information: 3 days / 24 hrs, Beginner to Intermediate, 2 hrs assessment.
--   * Funding validity 29 Aug 2023 - 28 Aug 2027; Absentee Payroll $4.50/hr.
--   * Skills Framework: Data Analytics (ICT-BIN-3104-1.1).
--   * Exam weightings from the official study guide, skills measured as of 20 Apr 2026.
--   * Practice-exam URL verified HTTP 200: https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/practice-exams/microsoft/microsoft-pl-300
--
-- Notes for future editors:
--  * apply.php splits statements on ";" at end-of-line — the content HTML below is ONE line.
--  * Idempotent: WHERE NOT EXISTS on url_key, INSERT IGNORE on tag links. Safe to re-run.
--  * SG-only guard via @mms_instance — the CTA course is SG WSQ, absent on MY/GH.
--  * hero_image_url is NOT set here (SQL cannot render one) — generate on prod post-deploy.

SET @is_sg := IF(@mms_instance = 'SG', 1, 0);

INSERT INTO `mmd_blog_post` (`title`, `url_key`, `excerpt`, `content`, `author`, `status`, `published_at`, `related_skus`, `source_sku`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `meta_keywords`, `linkedin_urn`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) SELECT 'PL-300 Power BI Data Analyst in Singapore: Exam Domains, Funding and Practice Exams', 'pl-300-power-bi-data-analyst-singapore-guide', 'PL-300 is the Microsoft credential for analysts who already build reports and want the associate-level credential. This guide walks the exam domains and their weightings, sets out exactly what you pay after WSQ funding &mdash; $708 nett, or $468 for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above &mdash; and shows what the 3 days course covers.', '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p><strong>PL-300</strong> is the Microsoft credential for analysts who already build reports and want the associate-level credential. This guide covers what the exam measures, what the 3 days WSQ course covers, and what you pay after SkillsFuture funding &mdash; <strong>$708</strong> for Singapore Citizens and PRs aged 21 and above, or <strong>$468</strong> for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above.</p></div><h2>Why PL-300 is worth sitting</h2><p>Power BI is the default reporting tool across a large share of Singapore enterprises, and most people using it are self-taught. That usually shows up in the same places: data models that do not scale, DAX that returns the wrong number at the wrong grain, and dashboards that nobody trusts. PL-300 is the credential that certifies you can do the whole job properly &mdash; prepare, model, visualise and secure.</p><ul><li><strong>The exam is evenly weighted across preparing, modelling and visualising data</strong>, so it certifies the full workflow rather than just chart-building.</li><li><strong>Data modelling and DAX are where self-taught analysts have the biggest gaps</strong>, and they carry 25&ndash;30% of the marks.</li><li><strong>Row-level security and workspace management are covered</strong> &mdash; the governance skills that separate a hobby report from a production one.</li><li><strong>Power BI Data Analyst is one of the most requested Microsoft credentials in Singapore analytics job listings.</strong></li></ul><p>The course is mapped to the Skills Framework under <strong>Data Analytics</strong> (TSC code ICT-BIN-3104-1.1), and leads to roles such as Data Analyst, Business Intelligence Specialist, Business Analyst, Data Visualization Specialist. <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-power-bi-data-analyst-associate-pl-300.html">Check the funding you qualify for</a>.</p><h2>The PL-300 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><td>Exam</td><td>PL-300: Microsoft Power BI Data Analyst</td></tr><tr><td>Length</td><td>100 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Passing score</td><td>700 out of 1000 (scaled &mdash; not 70%)</td></tr><tr><td>Certification</td><td>Power BI Data Analyst Associate</td></tr><tr><td>Renewal</td><td>Free online renewal every 12 months</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>PL-300 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>These are the skills measured on the official study guide. The weightings tell you where to spend your revision time.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Skills measured</th><th>Weighting</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Prepare the data</td><td>25&ndash;30%</td></tr><tr><td>Model the data</td><td>25&ndash;30%</td></tr><tr><td>Visualize and analyze the data</td><td>25&ndash;30%</td></tr><tr><td>Manage and secure Power BI</td><td>15&ndash;20%</td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>Source: official Microsoft study guide, skills measured as of 20 Apr 2026.</em></p><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>The 3 days (24 hrs) <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-power-bi-data-analyst-associate-pl-300.html"><strong>WSQ - Microsoft Power BI Data Analyst Associate (PL-300)</strong></a> course is pitched at <strong>Beginner to Intermediate</strong> level and is delivered in our Woodlands classroom with hands-on labs, followed by a 2 hrs assessment. The outline tracks the official objectives:</p><ol><li>Discover data analysis</li><li>Get started building with Power BI</li><li>Get data in Power BI</li><li>Clean, transform, and load data in Power BI</li><li>Design a data model in Power BI</li><li>Introduction to creating measures using DAX in Power BI</li><li>Optimize a model for performance in Power BI</li><li>Work with Power BI visuals</li><li>Create a data-driven story with Power BI reports</li><li>Create dashboards in Power BI</li><li>Work with AI visuals in Power BI</li><li>Create and manage workspaces in Power BI</li><li>Manage datasets in Power BI</li><li>Implement row-level security</li></ol><h2>Practise before you book the exam</h2><p>Course participants get free, unlimited access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/practice-exams/microsoft/microsoft-pl-300">PL-300 practice exams</a> on the Tertiary Infotech Practice Exam Portal, in both Practice Mode (with instant explanations) and timed Exam Mode. The portal offers non-participants 10 free questions per exam.</p><h2>What you actually pay: funding for PL-300 training</h2><p>The full fee is $1,200 before GST. As an SWDA-funded WSQ course, the subsidy depends on your citizenship, age and who is sponsoring you:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Who you are</th><th>Subsidy</th><th>You pay (incl. GST)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Non-funded / international participants</td><td>&ndash;</td><td>$1,308</td></tr><tr><td>Singapore Citizen or PR, aged 21 and above</td><td>50%</td><td><strong>$708</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Singapore Citizen aged 40 and above (MCES), or SME-sponsored</td><td>70%</td><td><strong>$468</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>GST of $108 is charged at 9% on the full course fee of $1,200, as required for SWDA-funded courses &mdash; the subsidy applies to the course fee, not the tax.</em></p><p>Funding for this course is valid from <strong>29 Aug 2023</strong> to <strong>28 Aug 2027</strong>. You must register and complete the course within that window to qualify.</p><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">1. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Singaporeans aged 25 and above have an opening SkillsFuture Credit of $500 plus any top-ups, and those aged 40 and above received a $4,000 Mid-Career top-up. Credit can offset the fee payable after subsidy, though the Mid-Career top-up cannot be used on this course. <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/how-to-claim-skillsfuture-credit.html">How to claim SkillsFuture Credit</a>.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">2. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Eligible employers can draw on SFEC to cover out-of-pocket costs when sponsoring staff. See our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/sfec.html">SFEC guide</a> for who qualifies and how to claim.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">3. PSEA</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Singapore Citizens can use Post-Secondary Education Account funds to offset the fee payable after subsidy. This course carries the PSEA tag, so it is eligible.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">4. UTAP</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>NTUC members can claim 50% of the unfunded fee under UTAP, capped at $250 a year, or $500 a year for members aged 40 and above. See the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/utap.html">UTAP guide</a>.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">5. Absentee Payroll</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Employers sponsoring staff can claim Absentee Payroll at $4.50 an hour, capped at $100,000 per enterprise per year, for the hours staff spend in training.</p></div></details></div><p><a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-power-bi-data-analyst-associate-pl-300.html"><strong>See the live fee breakdown for your profile &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Register for the 3 days WSQ course.</strong> Pick an intake on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-power-bi-data-analyst-associate-pl-300.html">course page</a> and apply your funding at checkout.</li><li><strong>Attend and complete the assessment.</strong> You need at least 75% attendance and a pass in the 2 hrs assessment to receive your WSQ Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Rehearse on the practice exams</strong> until you are consistently clearing the pass mark under timed conditions.</li><li><strong>Book and sit PL-300</strong> through Pearson VUE. The certification exam is booked and paid for separately from the course.</li></ol><h2>Where to go after PL-300</h2><p>For the enterprise analytics platform underneath, <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-certified-fabric-data-engineer-associate-dp-700-training.html">DP-700 on Microsoft Fabric</a> is the natural progression. If you want the data-platform fundamentals first, <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-azure-data-fundamentals-dp-900.html">DP-900</a> covers them. Browse the full <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/microsoft-certifications-exams.html">Microsoft certification course catalogue</a> to plan the next rung.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need Power BI experience before this course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Some familiarity helps &mdash; the course is pitched at beginner-to-intermediate level &mdash; but it starts from getting data in and builds up to modelling, DAX and security.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How much DAX does the exam cover?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>DAX sits inside the modelling domain, which carries 25&ndash;30% of the marks. It is a substantial part of the exam and the area most candidates underestimate.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the exam fee included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course covers training and the WSQ assessment; the PL-300 exam is booked separately through Pearson VUE.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Does PL-300 expire?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. Like all Microsoft role-based certifications, it renews every 12 months through a free, unproctored online assessment on Microsoft Learn.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>3 days (24 hours), followed by a 2-hour assessment.</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for Power BI Data Analyst training</h2><p>Seats are limited and classes fill ahead of each intake. View upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-microsoft-power-bi-data-analyst-associate-pl-300.html"><strong>WSQ - Microsoft Power BI Data Analyst Associate (PL-300)</strong></a> course page, or call us on +65 6100 0613 if you would like your funding worked out first.</p>', 'Tertiary Infotech Academy', 1, '2025-09-19', 'TGS-2023037468', 'TGS-2023037468', 'PL-300 Course Singapore | Power BI Data Analyst | WSQ Funding', 'Train for PL-300 Power BI Data Analyst in Singapore. 3 days WSQ course from $468 nett after funding, full exam domain breakdown, and free practice exams for participants.', 'pl-300 course singapore, power bi data analyst certification, pl-300 exam, wsq microsoft course, skillsfuture microsoft certification, microsoft certification singapore, pl-300 funding, pl-300 training singapore', 'manual-skip-no-share', '2025-09-19 09:00:00', '2025-09-19 09:00:00' FROM DUAL WHERE @is_sg > 0 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `mmd_blog_post` WHERE `url_key` = 'pl-300-power-bi-data-analyst-singapore-guide');

